e your  favorites but there's not a bad one in  the bunch  and having played eternal I got I got  the inside track that I know internal is  gonna be awesome  probably my personal favorite so that's  just the exciting thing I know this  brand is gonna continue it's gonna be  something that as long as we hold true  to these ideals over the originals we're  gonna we're gonna be on the right track  yet I just thank everybody for playing  and thank it guys for making a career  for a lot of us here because without it  we wouldn't have liked I thought games  were magic things that came out of Japan  like that's how they showed up right  like oh I didn't know I could make games  and I started learning to make levels  and humans like it's possible and  without that you know there's there's a  whole industry that wouldn't have  existed if you guys hadn't suffered  through the pain of moaning and  screaming Dennis tear people and and hit  so many thing it is fascinating how many  things you guys did right from mods to  the perfect balance of this it's you  know four and B in 25 years like this  generational and I love seeing people  are still making maps today you can go  and check out do maps that are  mind-blowing today that we just couldn't  even imagine back then because there's a  community that's still just building  these classic new maps it's fascinating  so yeah thanks to everybody here their  plays and again to you guys for making  it possible for us to be sitting here so  that's right  well that's our that's our panel thanks  everybody for joining us if you're here  at QuakeCon be sure to go down to the  exhibit hall  check out doom eternal play the classic  doom games and have a great quake on  thank you thank you guys  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

